WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.260
Imagine saving your company $10 million.

00:04.760 --> 00:05.320
That'd be nice.

00:05.460 --> 00:05.640
Right.

00:05.940 --> 00:07.560
You do all the math, you run the projections,

00:07.880 --> 00:10.440
and you basically prove that this highly anticipated,

00:10.640 --> 00:13.640
incredibly expensive new app is just,

00:13.860 --> 00:15.420
it's going to be an absolute disaster.

00:16.040 --> 00:16.740
A total train wreck.

00:16.880 --> 00:17.080
Yeah.

00:17.300 --> 00:18.920
So you stop the launch,

00:19.240 --> 00:22.320
you literally save the entire quarter for the company,

00:22.780 --> 00:24.060
and then at the end of the year,

00:24.160 --> 00:25.840
you sit there and watch the guy

00:25.840 --> 00:27.780
who designed the company's new logo

00:27.780 --> 00:29.460
get promoted instead of you.

00:29.460 --> 00:31.240
Yeah, which happens all the time.

00:31.360 --> 00:31.780
All the time.

00:32.120 --> 00:33.600
And, you know, why does that happen?

00:33.680 --> 00:36.300
It's because he produced a tangible artifact.

00:37.020 --> 00:38.500
He launched a thing.

00:38.620 --> 00:41.060
The system has a metric for things launched,

00:41.220 --> 00:43.440
but it has absolutely zero capacity

00:43.440 --> 00:45.340
to measure the profound value

00:45.340 --> 00:46.880
of the things you prevented from happening.

00:47.020 --> 00:48.080
It's completely blind to it.

00:48.160 --> 00:48.460
Exactly.

00:49.020 --> 00:50.380
So for today's deep dive,

00:50.480 --> 00:51.980
we are looking at this fascinating,

00:52.240 --> 00:55.820
honestly kind of dense white paper from August 2026.

00:56.320 --> 00:58.580
It's titled Rebel Without a Cost

00:58.580 --> 01:00.460
by the research group Flyxion.

01:00.760 --> 01:02.400
Yeah, it's a really brilliant piece of work.

01:02.740 --> 01:03.280
It is.

01:03.360 --> 01:06.940
And we are unpacking this central underlying mystery

01:06.940 --> 01:10.000
that governs almost all of our digital lives right now.

01:10.240 --> 01:12.620
Like, why is it that turning our hard work

01:12.620 --> 01:15.320
into a measurable token or a score

01:15.320 --> 01:18.940
inevitably destroys the value of the work itself?

01:18.940 --> 01:19.300
Right.

01:19.380 --> 01:20.900
And the premise Flyxion tackles here

01:20.900 --> 01:23.040
is just pervasive everywhere you look.

01:23.520 --> 01:25.860
I mean, we operate under this default assumption

01:25.860 --> 01:30.000
that human coordination naturally evolves

01:30.000 --> 01:30.880
toward tokenization.

01:31.040 --> 01:31.260
Right.

01:31.340 --> 01:32.600
Like everything needs a score.

01:32.780 --> 01:33.060
Exactly.

01:33.200 --> 01:34.440
You log into a developer forum,

01:34.500 --> 01:35.560
you get a reputation score,

01:35.720 --> 01:37.860
you contribute to an open source Web3 project,

01:37.980 --> 01:38.840
you get a governance token.

01:39.140 --> 01:41.540
We just assume that wrapping human effort

01:41.540 --> 01:44.300
in a quantifiable financialized container

01:44.300 --> 01:46.680
is basically an upgrade to human memory.

01:46.680 --> 01:48.240
But this paper is saying,

01:48.320 --> 01:49.940
well, they argue it's actually the opposite, right?

01:50.020 --> 01:51.960
Yeah, they argue it is a catastrophic downgrade.

01:52.060 --> 01:52.180
Yeah.

01:52.380 --> 01:54.600
They present this really rigorous mathematical

01:54.600 --> 01:56.040
and architectural proof

01:56.040 --> 01:58.140
showing that the tokenized self

01:58.140 --> 01:59.880
is not just flawed in practice.

02:00.520 --> 02:02.980
It's actually logically impossible to sustain

02:02.980 --> 02:04.540
without causing systemic harm.

02:04.800 --> 02:07.080
Which completely challenges the foundation

02:07.080 --> 02:10.540
of nearly every decentralized autonomous organization

02:10.540 --> 02:13.320
or DAO operating today.

02:13.480 --> 02:15.740
I mean, it pulls the rug right out from under them.

02:15.740 --> 02:16.500
It really does.

02:16.680 --> 02:18.680
So let's start with the feasibility study,

02:18.860 --> 02:19.660
the paper critiques,

02:19.800 --> 02:21.480
because I think it sets the stage perfectly.

02:21.640 --> 02:24.740
It's referred to as the Ahorian study.

02:24.960 --> 02:26.020
Yeah, the IAM project.

02:26.140 --> 02:26.320
Right.

02:26.540 --> 02:28.220
And this was a real world attempt

02:28.220 --> 02:31.420
to solve the classic free rider problem, right?

02:31.480 --> 02:34.620
Like communities realize that vital maintenance work

02:34.620 --> 02:36.280
goes completely unrecorded.

02:36.460 --> 02:37.300
Right, the invisible labor.

02:37.500 --> 02:37.940
Exactly.

02:38.400 --> 02:41.520
So the IAM study proposed this continuous pipeline.

02:41.920 --> 02:43.060
A contributor does the work,

02:43.160 --> 02:44.140
the system logs it,

02:44.320 --> 02:45.720
calculates a contribution score,

02:45.720 --> 02:47.540
mints a token based on that score,

02:47.720 --> 02:49.420
and just drops it into a wallet.

02:49.640 --> 02:50.620
Boom, you're rewarded.

02:50.840 --> 02:51.120
Boom.

02:51.740 --> 02:53.560
Suddenly, the person fixing the bugs

02:53.560 --> 02:55.420
holds a percentage of voting power

02:55.420 --> 02:56.840
over the entire network.

02:57.240 --> 02:58.820
And, you know, on its face,

02:58.860 --> 03:00.640
that sounds like a perfect meritocracy.

03:00.800 --> 03:01.240
It does.

03:01.320 --> 03:02.620
It sounds incredibly fair

03:02.620 --> 03:04.720
until you look at what's actually happening under the hood.

03:05.260 --> 03:07.500
The fatal flaw in the IAM system,

03:07.660 --> 03:08.320
according to Flyxion,

03:08.320 --> 03:11.200
is this phenomenon they call the Great Compression.

03:11.740 --> 03:12.500
The Great Compression.

03:12.660 --> 03:13.700
Okay, break that down for us.

03:13.780 --> 03:16.300
So by forcing that entire pipeline

03:16.300 --> 03:19.080
into a single smart contract or a single token,

03:19.680 --> 03:22.420
the system conflicts radically different categories

03:22.420 --> 03:23.300
of human judgment.

03:23.660 --> 03:24.860
Wait, meaning what exactly?

03:25.020 --> 03:27.240
Meaning you take documentary history,

03:27.620 --> 03:31.040
like the sheer objective fact that an event took place,

03:31.220 --> 03:33.180
and you crush it into economic value.

03:33.280 --> 03:34.180
Okay, I'm with you.

03:34.280 --> 03:35.740
And then you take that economic value

03:35.740 --> 03:38.160
and immediately crush it into political authority.

03:38.760 --> 03:40.460
The container holding all of this

03:40.460 --> 03:43.260
is just one single digital identity.

03:44.340 --> 03:47.780
The authors identify this as a profound category error.

03:47.900 --> 03:49.060
Okay, let's unpack this,

03:49.120 --> 03:51.660
because they introduced this chain of non-implications

03:51.660 --> 03:54.040
called the six acts that are not one act.

03:54.300 --> 03:55.740
And I really want to walk through these.

03:55.860 --> 03:57.020
It fundamentally breaks down

03:57.020 --> 03:59.900
how a healthy society actually processes information.

04:00.260 --> 04:02.260
Yeah, this is the core of their architectural argument.

04:02.260 --> 04:03.760
Right, so the sequence goes,

04:03.760 --> 04:07.760
record, verify, recognize, reward, authorize, and continue.

04:08.160 --> 04:10.420
And in our current digital infrastructure,

04:10.740 --> 04:13.100
these just bleed into one another constantly.

04:13.380 --> 04:16.200
But logically, one step does not imply the next.

04:16.360 --> 04:16.840
Not at all.

04:17.000 --> 04:18.060
Let's take the first two.

04:18.920 --> 04:20.720
Record does not imply verify.

04:21.600 --> 04:23.180
Think of it like getting a receipt

04:23.180 --> 04:24.480
for buying a microphone on Amazon.

04:24.700 --> 04:25.400
That's the record.

04:25.880 --> 04:27.440
But that receipt doesn't verify

04:27.440 --> 04:29.220
that the microphone actually works.

04:29.340 --> 04:29.760
Exactly.

04:29.760 --> 04:32.860
Or if I submit a patch to a shared code base,

04:33.440 --> 04:36.400
the system records that I uploaded a file at 2 p.m.

04:36.660 --> 04:38.700
That is mere data entry.

04:38.940 --> 04:39.900
Right, it's just a log.

04:40.080 --> 04:43.220
Verification is an entirely separate evidentiary process.

04:43.920 --> 04:44.940
Does the code compile?

04:45.500 --> 04:46.940
Does it pass security checks?

04:47.360 --> 04:49.900
Did it actually do what the commit message claimed?

04:50.100 --> 04:51.360
Which is a whole different ballgame.

04:51.360 --> 04:54.120
And then the distinction becomes even more critical

04:54.120 --> 04:56.260
when we move from verify to recognize.

04:57.020 --> 05:00.060
Because getting a receipt isn't a five-star review.

05:00.220 --> 05:00.360
Right.

05:00.640 --> 05:02.480
Because verification is factual.

05:02.660 --> 05:02.880
Okay.

05:03.020 --> 05:04.860
But recognition is normative and social.

05:05.040 --> 05:06.180
Okay, give me an example of that.

05:06.220 --> 05:07.840
Well, we can mathematically prove

05:07.840 --> 05:10.140
that an individual deleted every single file

05:10.140 --> 05:11.060
in a shared directory.

05:11.180 --> 05:11.560
Oh, wow.

05:11.740 --> 05:12.980
Yeah, definitely verifiable.

05:13.380 --> 05:13.560
Right.

05:13.620 --> 05:16.540
The system verifies the action flawlessly.

05:16.540 --> 05:21.160
However, the community will absolutely not recognize

05:21.160 --> 05:23.280
that action as a valuable contribution.

05:24.260 --> 05:26.780
We frequently mistake the ability to measure an action

05:26.780 --> 05:29.300
for the community's endorsement of that action.

05:29.520 --> 05:30.760
Yeah, just because you can track it

05:30.760 --> 05:31.680
doesn't mean it's good.

05:32.600 --> 05:34.820
Which brings us to the leap that trips up

05:34.820 --> 05:37.580
almost every corporate environment and online community.

05:38.560 --> 05:40.540
Recognize does not imply reward,

05:41.000 --> 05:44.400
and reward absolutely does not imply authorize.

05:44.400 --> 05:46.280
This is where the wheels really come off

05:46.280 --> 05:47.420
in tokenized systems.

05:47.640 --> 05:48.040
Exactly.

05:48.260 --> 05:49.900
Like, if I hire an independent contractor

05:49.900 --> 05:51.140
to fix a company server,

05:51.600 --> 05:52.880
they execute the job perfectly.

05:53.020 --> 05:54.780
The record is clear, the work is verified,

05:55.040 --> 05:56.220
I recognize their skill,

05:56.380 --> 05:58.100
and I reward them by paying their invoice.

05:58.340 --> 05:59.560
The transaction is complete.

05:59.720 --> 05:59.960
Right.

06:00.280 --> 06:02.500
But paying that invoice doesn't suddenly mean

06:02.500 --> 06:03.440
they should be the CEO.

06:03.880 --> 06:05.620
It doesn't authorize them to dictate

06:05.620 --> 06:06.760
the direction of the company.

06:07.440 --> 06:09.840
Yet, in DAOs, the moment you get a token

06:09.840 --> 06:10.900
for doing a job,

06:11.280 --> 06:12.840
you are simultaneously authorized

06:12.840 --> 06:14.060
to govern the protocol.

06:14.060 --> 06:16.140
Which is wild when you think about it,

06:16.220 --> 06:17.440
because historically,

06:17.880 --> 06:20.120
human beings have spent centuries

06:20.120 --> 06:21.760
constructing institutions

06:21.760 --> 06:24.660
specifically designed to keep these six acts

06:24.660 --> 06:25.860
isolated from one another.

06:26.060 --> 06:26.760
We have.

06:26.980 --> 06:27.440
Like what?

06:27.780 --> 06:29.060
Think about a public library.

06:29.680 --> 06:31.480
It's a perfect example of isolating

06:31.480 --> 06:33.280
the record and verify functions

06:33.280 --> 06:35.120
from recognition and authority.

06:35.700 --> 06:38.520
A library will maintain an archive of books

06:38.520 --> 06:40.140
promoting, you know,

06:40.200 --> 06:43.100
entirely discredited pseudoscientific theories.

06:43.100 --> 06:43.340
Right.

06:43.480 --> 06:45.500
You can find flat earth books in a library.

06:45.820 --> 06:46.120
Exactly.

06:46.580 --> 06:48.580
The institution preserves the historical record

06:48.580 --> 06:49.700
so we know it was said.

06:50.300 --> 06:52.080
But the presence of the book on this shelf

06:52.080 --> 06:54.440
is not an institutional endorsement of the theory.

06:54.880 --> 06:57.100
The boundaries protect the integrity of the archive.

06:57.300 --> 06:58.460
Oh, that makes so much sense.

06:58.560 --> 06:59.660
We see the same boundary management

06:59.660 --> 07:01.060
in professional credentials, right?

07:01.440 --> 07:04.160
Like, a highly specialized cardiothoracic surgeon

07:04.160 --> 07:06.580
wields absolute unquestioned authority

07:06.580 --> 07:07.960
inside an operating room.

07:07.960 --> 07:09.940
Literal life and death authority, yeah.

07:10.400 --> 07:10.540
Right.

07:10.680 --> 07:12.220
Their past merit dictates

07:12.220 --> 07:13.680
their current operational power

07:13.680 --> 07:15.200
in that specific context.

07:15.820 --> 07:16.900
But if that same surgeon

07:16.900 --> 07:18.260
attends a town hall meeting

07:18.260 --> 07:19.620
to debate zoning laws

07:19.620 --> 07:20.840
for a new commercial development,

07:21.360 --> 07:22.680
their medical credentials

07:22.680 --> 07:24.620
do not grant them an extra hundred votes.

07:24.740 --> 07:24.880
Right.

07:25.160 --> 07:26.480
Because their past merit

07:26.480 --> 07:27.620
does not translate

07:27.620 --> 07:29.940
into universal general authority.

07:30.160 --> 07:32.060
And so the fundamental danger

07:32.060 --> 07:33.540
of a tokenized system

07:33.540 --> 07:35.800
is that it mints a single asset

07:35.800 --> 07:37.840
that just travels effortlessly

07:37.840 --> 07:39.840
across all six of these acts.

07:40.060 --> 07:41.820
It completely obliterates

07:41.820 --> 07:42.960
the contextual boundaries

07:42.960 --> 07:45.060
that make functional governance possible

07:45.060 --> 07:46.100
in the real world.

07:46.300 --> 07:47.340
Yeah, the authors argue

07:47.340 --> 07:48.960
that our architectural imperative

07:48.960 --> 07:49.920
should not be

07:49.920 --> 07:52.760
how do we extract financial value

07:52.760 --> 07:53.880
from every human action?

07:54.460 --> 07:54.840
It should be

07:54.840 --> 07:56.380
how do we prevent the nuance

07:56.380 --> 07:57.340
of human history

07:57.340 --> 07:58.760
from being erased

07:58.760 --> 08:00.520
by the mechanisms of finance?

08:00.820 --> 08:02.260
I can hear a systems engineer

08:02.260 --> 08:03.320
listening to this right now

08:03.320 --> 08:03.700
and arguing,

08:03.840 --> 08:03.960
you know,

08:04.000 --> 08:05.640
the problem isn't the token itself.

08:06.100 --> 08:06.940
The problem is just

08:06.940 --> 08:08.260
the crudeness of the algorithm.

08:08.440 --> 08:08.780
Oh, yeah.

08:08.820 --> 08:09.420
The classic

08:09.420 --> 08:11.500
we just need better math argument.

08:12.120 --> 08:12.600
Exactly.

08:12.740 --> 08:13.880
The pushback is always,

08:14.060 --> 08:15.200
well, if the token

08:15.200 --> 08:16.400
is creating bad governance,

08:16.400 --> 08:16.980
we just need

08:16.980 --> 08:17.740
a more sophisticated

08:17.740 --> 08:18.840
reputation score.

08:19.240 --> 08:19.900
We need to weigh

08:19.900 --> 08:21.120
different actions differently

08:21.120 --> 08:22.660
and create a perfectly

08:22.660 --> 08:23.900
accurate leaderboard.

08:24.380 --> 08:25.640
But Flyxion anticipates

08:25.640 --> 08:26.600
that exact argument.

08:27.380 --> 08:28.740
They completely dismantle it

08:28.740 --> 08:30.500
using order-theoretic mathematics.

08:31.340 --> 08:31.780
Specifically,

08:32.160 --> 08:32.900
they look at

08:32.900 --> 08:34.120
partially ordered sets

08:34.120 --> 08:35.040
or plus-its.

08:35.580 --> 08:36.560
They introduce this thing

08:36.560 --> 08:37.940
called Proposition 1,

08:38.480 --> 08:39.660
the non-canonicity

08:39.660 --> 08:41.160
of total contribution rankings.

08:41.160 --> 08:41.640
Okay.

08:41.780 --> 08:42.720
We're definitely going to need

08:42.720 --> 08:44.260
to define some of those terms.

08:44.560 --> 08:45.800
What is the non-canonicity

08:45.800 --> 08:47.260
of total contribution rankings?

08:47.260 --> 08:48.800
So the underlying math here

08:48.800 --> 08:49.920
exposes the lie

08:49.920 --> 08:51.380
of the universal leaderboard.

08:51.960 --> 08:52.820
Human contributions

08:52.820 --> 08:54.900
within any complex project

08:54.900 --> 08:56.860
form a partially ordered set.

08:57.260 --> 08:57.560
That means,

08:57.900 --> 08:58.660
while some actions

08:58.660 --> 08:59.900
can be directly compared

08:59.900 --> 09:00.460
and ranked,

09:00.820 --> 09:01.840
the entire set

09:01.840 --> 09:02.600
is heterogeneous.

09:02.980 --> 09:04.300
So it's apples and oranges?

09:04.640 --> 09:05.140
Basically.

09:05.520 --> 09:06.420
Think of an anti-chain

09:06.420 --> 09:07.060
in mathematics.

09:07.340 --> 09:08.740
It's a subset of elements

09:08.740 --> 09:09.880
where no two elements

09:09.880 --> 09:10.760
are actually comparable.

09:11.020 --> 09:13.260
Let's ground that anti-chain concept

09:13.260 --> 09:15.160
in a real-world software project.

09:15.160 --> 09:17.040
Say you have developer A, right?

09:17.600 --> 09:19.800
They spend three intense weeks

09:19.800 --> 09:22.000
rewriting the database query logic

09:22.000 --> 09:24.240
to reduce latency by 40%.

09:24.240 --> 09:25.080
A massive,

09:25.300 --> 09:26.860
highly technical achievement.

09:27.100 --> 09:27.640
Massive.

09:27.800 --> 09:28.480
But then you have

09:28.480 --> 09:29.860
community manager B.

09:30.640 --> 09:32.080
Over those same three weeks,

09:32.180 --> 09:32.960
a toxic,

09:33.260 --> 09:34.720
factional dispute erupts

09:34.720 --> 09:36.000
among the core maintainers

09:36.000 --> 09:37.020
that threatens to fork

09:37.020 --> 09:38.060
the entire project.

09:38.640 --> 09:39.540
Community manager B

09:39.540 --> 09:40.980
successfully mediates

09:40.980 --> 09:41.580
the dispute,

09:42.040 --> 09:43.220
de-escalates the tension,

09:43.220 --> 09:45.100
and keeps the team intact.

09:45.280 --> 09:46.660
Also critical to the survival

09:46.660 --> 09:47.320
of the project.

09:47.460 --> 09:47.640
Right.

09:47.760 --> 09:48.840
So if we are trying to build

09:48.840 --> 09:49.940
a perfectly accurate

09:49.940 --> 09:51.000
reputation score,

09:51.740 --> 09:53.220
how on earth do we rank

09:53.220 --> 09:54.340
those two contributions

09:54.340 --> 09:55.380
against each other?

09:55.540 --> 09:56.800
The mathematical reality

09:56.800 --> 09:58.180
is that they are incomparable.

09:58.500 --> 09:59.420
They occupy entirely

09:59.420 --> 10:00.200
different domains.

10:00.480 --> 10:01.340
They require completely

10:01.340 --> 10:02.220
different skill sets

10:02.220 --> 10:03.820
and they impact the project

10:03.820 --> 10:04.940
along different vectors.

10:05.080 --> 10:05.900
So you can't rank them?

10:06.160 --> 10:07.380
You mathematically cannot.

10:08.060 --> 10:09.620
The order extension theorem

10:09.620 --> 10:10.820
dictates that when you have

10:10.820 --> 10:12.020
incomparable elements

10:12.020 --> 10:13.440
within a partially ordered set,

10:13.800 --> 10:14.720
there are multiple

10:14.720 --> 10:16.120
equally valid ways

10:16.120 --> 10:16.980
to force them

10:16.980 --> 10:18.040
into a linear sequence.

10:18.400 --> 10:19.040
You could rank

10:19.040 --> 10:20.040
the database rewrite

10:20.040 --> 10:21.000
above the mediation

10:21.000 --> 10:22.580
or the mediation

10:22.580 --> 10:23.440
above the rewrite.

10:23.880 --> 10:24.920
And the data doesn't tell you

10:24.920 --> 10:25.720
which one is right.

10:25.940 --> 10:26.420
Exactly.

10:26.660 --> 10:28.180
The empirical documentary record

10:28.180 --> 10:29.380
provides zero data

10:29.380 --> 10:30.500
to resolve that tie.

10:30.620 --> 10:31.060
But wait,

10:31.160 --> 10:32.300
from a practical standpoint,

10:32.520 --> 10:33.880
if I am a hiring manager

10:33.880 --> 10:34.940
or if I'm allocating

10:34.940 --> 10:36.260
a fixed quarterly budget,

10:36.980 --> 10:38.260
I don't really have the luxury

10:38.260 --> 10:39.680
of calling things incomparable.

10:39.840 --> 10:40.800
I have to make a decision.

10:40.960 --> 10:41.720
I have to rank them.

10:42.020 --> 10:43.520
Even if a scalar score

10:43.520 --> 10:45.460
like a single numerical value

10:45.460 --> 10:46.700
is flawed,

10:47.080 --> 10:48.520
isn't it a necessary heuristic

10:48.520 --> 10:49.920
just to operate at scale?

10:50.160 --> 10:51.020
Well, the necessity

10:51.020 --> 10:52.020
of making a decision

10:52.020 --> 10:53.000
does not validate

10:53.000 --> 10:54.320
the mathematical integrity

10:54.320 --> 10:54.880
of the score.

10:55.480 --> 10:56.480
This is a crucial point.

10:56.940 --> 10:58.060
When a scalar system

10:58.060 --> 10:59.020
forces a ranking

10:59.020 --> 11:00.600
between incomparable actions,

11:00.720 --> 11:02.480
say it assigns 98 points

11:02.480 --> 11:03.080
to the developer

11:03.080 --> 11:03.980
and 95 points

11:03.980 --> 11:04.680
to the mediator,

11:05.200 --> 11:06.400
it is not discovering

11:06.400 --> 11:07.160
a hidden truth

11:07.160 --> 11:07.880
about the universe.

11:08.440 --> 11:09.300
What is it doing then?

11:09.300 --> 11:10.640
It is manufacturing

11:10.640 --> 11:11.900
and institutional bias

11:11.900 --> 11:13.180
and presenting it

11:13.180 --> 11:13.980
as objective data.

11:13.980 --> 11:15.100
Oh, wow.

11:15.360 --> 11:16.380
Manufacturing bias.

11:16.540 --> 11:16.780
Yes.

11:17.420 --> 11:18.080
By stripping away

11:18.080 --> 11:18.740
the context

11:18.740 --> 11:20.040
to produce a single number,

11:20.360 --> 11:21.640
the algorithm destroys

11:21.640 --> 11:22.680
the very information

11:22.680 --> 11:23.540
required to make

11:23.540 --> 11:24.480
an informed judgment.

11:25.520 --> 11:26.460
The paper asserts

11:26.460 --> 11:26.980
that a system

11:26.980 --> 11:28.460
acknowledging incomparability

11:28.460 --> 11:29.920
is structurally honest.

11:30.700 --> 11:31.760
A system that forces

11:31.760 --> 11:33.680
a strict universal leaderboard

11:33.680 --> 11:35.240
is structurally lying.

11:35.240 --> 11:37.120
Structurally lying,

11:37.320 --> 11:38.000
which sets up

11:38.000 --> 11:40.960
this catastrophic failure cascade

11:40.960 --> 11:42.540
when you attach financial value

11:42.540 --> 11:43.440
to that structurally

11:43.440 --> 11:44.360
dishonest score.

11:44.440 --> 11:44.880
Exactly.

11:45.160 --> 11:45.740
Which is what

11:45.740 --> 11:47.100
almost all VAOs do.

11:47.200 --> 11:47.480
Right.

11:47.840 --> 11:49.300
The AAN feasibility study

11:49.300 --> 11:50.740
didn't just want to rank people.

11:51.040 --> 11:51.960
It wanted to distribute

11:51.960 --> 11:53.400
tradable governance tokens

11:53.400 --> 11:54.680
based on those rankings.

11:55.180 --> 11:55.840
And this brings us

11:55.840 --> 11:56.800
to proposition two,

11:57.240 --> 11:58.880
the transfer fidelity conflict.

11:59.040 --> 11:59.860
And the logical proof

11:59.860 --> 12:00.660
they used to demonstrate

12:00.660 --> 12:01.280
this conflict

12:01.280 --> 12:02.060
is devastating

12:02.060 --> 12:03.320
to the entire concept

12:03.320 --> 12:04.040
of tokenomics,

12:04.040 --> 12:05.440
especially the idea

12:05.440 --> 12:06.320
of skin in the game.

12:06.460 --> 12:06.960
How so?

12:07.340 --> 12:08.420
Break down the proof for us.

12:08.600 --> 12:09.660
The proof outlines

12:09.660 --> 12:11.060
an impossible trolemma.

12:12.420 --> 12:13.260
Assume the system

12:13.260 --> 12:14.720
issues a governance token

12:14.720 --> 12:15.300
to Alice

12:15.300 --> 12:16.360
as a reward

12:16.360 --> 12:17.380
for her verified,

12:17.780 --> 12:18.960
high-quality contributions.

12:19.780 --> 12:21.120
The core philosophy

12:21.120 --> 12:21.740
of the system

12:21.740 --> 12:23.200
is that governance power

12:23.200 --> 12:24.000
should reside

12:24.000 --> 12:24.980
with those who have

12:24.980 --> 12:26.160
demonstrated competence

12:26.160 --> 12:28.120
and assumed responsibility, right?

12:28.240 --> 12:29.660
Yeah, that is the stated goal

12:29.660 --> 12:30.500
of almost every

12:30.500 --> 12:31.700
decentralized protocol.

12:31.860 --> 12:32.700
You earn your say.

12:32.800 --> 12:33.020
Right.

12:33.020 --> 12:34.880
The contradiction arises

12:34.880 --> 12:36.340
the moment Alice decides

12:36.340 --> 12:37.540
to leverage the financial

12:37.540 --> 12:38.440
aspect of the token.

12:38.580 --> 12:38.820
Oh.

12:39.020 --> 12:39.980
The token is an asset.

12:40.160 --> 12:40.860
It has liquidity.

12:41.580 --> 12:43.900
So Alice sells her token

12:43.900 --> 12:44.940
on an open exchange

12:44.940 --> 12:45.440
to Bob.

12:45.680 --> 12:46.000
Okay.

12:46.180 --> 12:47.360
Now Bob holds the token,

12:47.900 --> 12:48.980
which means Bob holds

12:48.980 --> 12:49.880
the governance power.

12:50.740 --> 12:52.500
But Bob has zero

12:52.500 --> 12:53.640
historical context

12:53.640 --> 12:54.560
within the project.

12:55.260 --> 12:56.220
Bob has not demonstrated

12:56.220 --> 12:57.500
any technical competence.

12:58.020 --> 12:58.820
Bob has not assumed

12:58.820 --> 12:59.640
any of the ongoing

12:59.640 --> 13:00.260
responsibilities

13:00.260 --> 13:01.080
that Alice

13:01.080 --> 13:02.360
originally undertook.

13:02.360 --> 13:03.200
He simply utilized

13:03.200 --> 13:04.240
capital to bypass

13:04.240 --> 13:05.320
the acts of record,

13:05.500 --> 13:06.720
verify, and recognize.

13:06.780 --> 13:07.160
Exactly.

13:07.280 --> 13:08.140
He just bought his way

13:08.140 --> 13:09.000
to the authorized step.

13:09.200 --> 13:09.960
Here's where it gets

13:09.960 --> 13:10.820
really interesting for me

13:10.820 --> 13:11.840
because this is the equivalent

13:11.840 --> 13:13.280
of purchasing a medical degree.

13:13.460 --> 13:14.180
That's a great way

13:14.180 --> 13:14.580
to put it.

13:14.800 --> 13:15.060
Right.

13:15.060 --> 13:16.700
The prestige and authority

13:16.700 --> 13:18.200
of an MD is built

13:18.200 --> 13:19.520
on years of verified

13:19.520 --> 13:20.680
clinical rotations,

13:21.000 --> 13:21.920
grueling exams,

13:22.060 --> 13:22.680
all of that.

13:23.020 --> 13:23.740
If the university

13:23.740 --> 13:24.620
suddenly allowed

13:24.620 --> 13:25.620
an exhausted resident

13:25.620 --> 13:26.660
to sell their MD

13:26.660 --> 13:28.180
to a wealthy individual

13:28.180 --> 13:29.180
who had literally

13:29.180 --> 13:31.080
never taken a biology class,

13:31.620 --> 13:33.200
the entire medical system

13:33.200 --> 13:34.100
would instantly

13:34.100 --> 13:35.060
lose its fidelity.

13:35.060 --> 13:35.980
It would collapse

13:35.980 --> 13:37.120
overnight because

13:37.120 --> 13:37.800
the convenience

13:37.800 --> 13:39.180
of the financial transaction

13:39.180 --> 13:40.860
requires the destruction

13:40.860 --> 13:42.400
of the historical context.

13:42.620 --> 13:43.220
The convenience

13:43.220 --> 13:44.440
requires the destruction.

13:44.620 --> 13:45.380
That is heavy.

13:45.600 --> 13:46.080
It is.

13:46.440 --> 13:47.400
And that mechanism

13:47.400 --> 13:48.060
of destruction

13:48.060 --> 13:49.160
leads Fulseria

13:49.160 --> 13:49.820
to propose

13:49.820 --> 13:51.420
a radical redefinition

13:51.420 --> 13:51.980
of currency.

13:52.420 --> 13:53.120
They define money

13:53.120 --> 13:54.220
not as the opposite

13:54.220 --> 13:54.860
of a ledger,

13:55.260 --> 13:56.780
but as an amputated ledger.

13:56.920 --> 13:58.080
An amputated ledger?

13:58.120 --> 13:58.400
Oh, wait.

13:58.480 --> 13:59.440
That is a phenomenal

13:59.440 --> 14:00.460
conceptual shift.

14:00.580 --> 14:01.480
We usually think of money

14:01.480 --> 14:02.380
as pure value,

14:02.380 --> 14:03.600
but they're framing it

14:03.600 --> 14:04.320
as a deliberate

14:04.320 --> 14:05.640
deletion of data.

14:06.060 --> 14:06.080
Yes.

14:06.600 --> 14:07.540
Consider just a physical

14:07.540 --> 14:08.120
dollar bill.

14:08.120 --> 14:09.440
When a transaction

14:09.440 --> 14:10.640
occurs using a dollar,

14:10.900 --> 14:12.120
the currency provides

14:12.120 --> 14:13.000
ultimate liquidity

14:13.000 --> 14:14.160
precisely because

14:14.160 --> 14:15.640
it enforces total amnesia.

14:15.860 --> 14:16.000
Amnesia.

14:16.020 --> 14:16.700
Think about it.

14:17.380 --> 14:18.480
The dollar does not

14:18.480 --> 14:19.740
record the labor conditions

14:19.740 --> 14:20.760
under which it was earned.

14:21.240 --> 14:22.160
It does not carry

14:22.160 --> 14:23.560
the history of the obligations

14:23.560 --> 14:24.800
it previously discharged.

14:25.340 --> 14:26.500
It does not indicate

14:26.500 --> 14:27.680
whether the current holder

14:27.680 --> 14:28.380
obtained it

14:28.380 --> 14:29.680
through technical brilliance,

14:30.080 --> 14:30.640
sheer luck,

14:30.780 --> 14:32.040
or malicious extraction.

14:32.100 --> 14:32.280
Right.

14:32.340 --> 14:32.900
It doesn't care.

14:33.300 --> 14:34.840
To make currency fungible,

14:34.980 --> 14:36.420
meaning any one unit

14:36.420 --> 14:37.860
is perfectly interchangeable

14:37.860 --> 14:38.960
with any other unit,

14:39.580 --> 14:40.580
you must structurally

14:40.580 --> 14:41.780
amputate its history.

14:41.980 --> 14:42.920
So fungibility

14:42.920 --> 14:44.180
requires forgetting.

14:44.440 --> 14:44.840
Exactly.

14:44.980 --> 14:46.300
So if your community's goal

14:46.300 --> 14:47.660
is to accurately remember

14:47.660 --> 14:48.480
who did what

14:48.480 --> 14:50.040
and to allocate authority

14:50.040 --> 14:51.680
based on that rich tapestry

14:51.680 --> 14:53.100
of historical contribution,

14:53.740 --> 14:54.960
the single most destructive

14:54.960 --> 14:55.940
action you can take

14:55.940 --> 14:57.500
is to convert that memory

14:57.500 --> 14:59.020
into a liquid token.

14:59.220 --> 15:01.120
You are actively choosing amnesia

15:01.120 --> 15:02.840
while operating under the delusion

15:02.840 --> 15:04.160
that you are optimizing memory.

15:04.360 --> 15:04.760
Wow.

15:04.760 --> 15:06.760
And a prior art on this topic

15:06.760 --> 15:07.840
is extensive, right?

15:08.040 --> 15:10.120
We already rely on massive

15:10.120 --> 15:11.220
planet-scale systems

15:11.220 --> 15:12.660
that function explicitly

15:12.660 --> 15:14.420
as ledgers without value.

15:14.700 --> 15:15.060
We do.

15:15.580 --> 15:16.560
Wikipedia is perhaps

15:16.560 --> 15:18.280
the most robust example of this.

15:18.600 --> 15:19.640
The platform maintains

15:19.640 --> 15:21.880
an exhaustive page history mechanism.

15:22.440 --> 15:23.600
Every single keystroke,

15:23.760 --> 15:25.180
every addition and deletion

15:25.180 --> 15:26.320
by every contributor

15:26.320 --> 15:27.780
is immutably recorded

15:27.780 --> 15:29.380
and publicly verifiable.

15:29.700 --> 15:31.080
But the Wikipedia architecture

15:31.080 --> 15:32.500
strictly separates

15:32.500 --> 15:33.820
that documentary record

15:33.820 --> 15:35.320
from operational authority.

15:35.640 --> 15:35.720
Right.

15:35.760 --> 15:36.940
Like, if I spend six months

15:36.940 --> 15:39.280
fixing 10,000 punctuation errors

15:39.280 --> 15:40.820
across historical articles,

15:41.060 --> 15:43.100
my edit count will be massive.

15:43.360 --> 15:43.660
Huge.

15:43.780 --> 15:45.340
The system records it perfectly.

15:45.860 --> 15:47.100
But that high edit count

15:47.100 --> 15:48.720
does not automatically trigger

15:48.720 --> 15:49.600
a smart contract

15:49.600 --> 15:50.480
that promotes me

15:50.480 --> 15:51.860
to a Wikipedia administrator.

15:51.960 --> 15:53.380
No, because admin status

15:53.380 --> 15:55.080
is an operational role.

15:55.080 --> 15:57.160
It requires a completely separate

15:57.160 --> 15:58.780
deliberative social process.

15:59.700 --> 16:00.820
The community must review

16:00.820 --> 16:01.980
the nature of your edits,

16:02.140 --> 16:03.160
your communication style

16:03.160 --> 16:03.980
on the talk pages,

16:04.400 --> 16:05.000
your understanding

16:05.000 --> 16:06.320
of consensus policies.

16:06.440 --> 16:07.240
It's not automated.

16:07.380 --> 16:08.240
And the same separation

16:08.240 --> 16:09.540
exists in Git too, right?

16:09.660 --> 16:11.040
The version control architecture

16:11.040 --> 16:12.260
underlying modern

16:12.260 --> 16:13.100
software engineering.

16:13.220 --> 16:13.340
Right.

16:13.480 --> 16:14.800
Git is a content address

16:14.800 --> 16:15.600
tracking system.

16:15.920 --> 16:17.200
It cryptographically secured

16:17.200 --> 16:18.100
every commit you make.

16:18.520 --> 16:19.540
The documentary record

16:19.540 --> 16:20.240
is pristine.

16:20.540 --> 16:21.840
But no matter how many lines

16:21.840 --> 16:22.680
of code I push

16:22.680 --> 16:23.680
to my local branch,

16:24.160 --> 16:25.200
that raw metric

16:25.200 --> 16:26.240
does not grant me

16:26.240 --> 16:26.900
the authorization

16:26.900 --> 16:28.100
to merge my code

16:28.100 --> 16:29.560
into the master repository

16:29.560 --> 16:31.360
of, say, the Linux kernel.

16:32.340 --> 16:32.920
Right access

16:32.920 --> 16:34.900
is an entirely distinct,

16:35.340 --> 16:37.020
manually governed layer.

16:37.260 --> 16:37.720
Exactly.

16:38.260 --> 16:39.180
And we can also look

16:39.180 --> 16:40.140
at the systemic failures

16:40.140 --> 16:40.700
that occur

16:40.700 --> 16:41.900
when this separation

16:41.900 --> 16:42.560
is breached.

16:43.100 --> 16:44.640
The academic publishing industry

16:44.640 --> 16:45.760
provides a really glaring

16:45.760 --> 16:46.860
cautionary tale here.

16:46.900 --> 16:48.220
Oh, the citation metrics?

16:48.460 --> 16:48.720
Yes.

16:49.260 --> 16:49.680
Originally,

16:49.820 --> 16:50.660
academic citations

16:50.660 --> 16:51.360
functioned purely

16:51.360 --> 16:52.540
as a documentary record.

16:52.960 --> 16:53.620
It was a map

16:53.620 --> 16:54.740
showing how one piece

16:54.740 --> 16:55.720
of research engaged

16:55.720 --> 16:56.660
with prior literature.

16:56.660 --> 16:58.020
It was a web of context.

16:58.380 --> 16:59.220
But then universities

16:59.220 --> 17:00.300
and funding bodies

17:00.300 --> 17:02.460
demanded a quantifiable metric

17:02.460 --> 17:03.740
to streamline hiring

17:03.740 --> 17:04.980
and grant distribution.

17:05.680 --> 17:06.260
They introduced

17:06.260 --> 17:07.200
scalar scores

17:07.200 --> 17:08.440
like the H-index

17:08.440 --> 17:10.120
and the journal impact factor.

17:10.240 --> 17:10.860
They compressed

17:10.860 --> 17:12.060
the documentary record

17:12.060 --> 17:13.400
into a performance metric.

17:13.540 --> 17:13.920
Exactly.

17:14.120 --> 17:14.740
And the distortion

17:14.740 --> 17:15.780
was instantaneous.

17:16.380 --> 17:17.080
Goodhart's law

17:17.080 --> 17:18.300
takes effect immediately.

17:18.820 --> 17:19.620
The moment a measure

17:19.620 --> 17:20.360
becomes a target,

17:20.540 --> 17:21.440
it ceases to be

17:21.440 --> 17:21.980
a good measure.

17:22.360 --> 17:22.680
Right.

17:23.040 --> 17:24.400
The metrics reform literature

17:24.400 --> 17:26.040
documents how researchers

17:26.040 --> 17:27.160
began optimizing

17:27.160 --> 17:28.080
for the score

17:28.080 --> 17:29.580
rather than the science.

17:30.360 --> 17:31.120
We saw the rise

17:31.120 --> 17:32.440
of citation cartels

17:32.440 --> 17:33.440
where academics

17:33.440 --> 17:34.780
artificially inflate

17:34.780 --> 17:35.600
each other's metrics.

17:35.740 --> 17:36.880
Which is just wild!

17:37.140 --> 17:38.780
And we saw a severe drop

17:38.780 --> 17:40.040
in replication studies.

17:40.600 --> 17:41.680
Because replicating

17:41.680 --> 17:42.720
existing work

17:42.720 --> 17:43.640
doesn't generate

17:43.640 --> 17:45.480
the same age index boost

17:45.480 --> 17:46.680
as publishing a novel,

17:47.180 --> 17:47.740
even if it's

17:47.740 --> 17:49.820
a statistically flimsy finding.

17:49.820 --> 17:51.320
So the academic crisis

17:51.320 --> 17:52.460
perfectly mirrors

17:52.460 --> 17:53.640
the governance collapse

17:53.640 --> 17:55.540
we see in tokenized ecosystems.

17:55.760 --> 17:57.180
It's the exact same failure mode.

17:57.420 --> 17:58.460
Okay, so if we accept

17:58.460 --> 17:58.940
the premise

17:58.940 --> 18:00.440
that tokens destroy context

18:00.440 --> 18:02.120
and scores manufacture bias,

18:02.300 --> 18:03.520
we run into a massive

18:03.520 --> 18:04.620
architectural problem

18:04.620 --> 18:05.520
regarding identity.

18:05.620 --> 18:06.320
Right, how do you know

18:06.320 --> 18:06.920
who anyone is?

18:06.960 --> 18:08.180
Right, because in current

18:08.180 --> 18:09.200
Web3 paradigms,

18:09.300 --> 18:10.140
your identity is

18:10.140 --> 18:11.260
inextricably linked

18:11.260 --> 18:11.920
to your wallet.

18:12.200 --> 18:13.060
Your standing in the community

18:13.060 --> 18:14.140
is literally the sum

18:14.140 --> 18:15.280
of the assets you hold.

18:15.580 --> 18:16.760
If we strip away

18:16.760 --> 18:17.900
the tokens and the scores,

18:17.900 --> 18:19.560
what exactly is

18:19.560 --> 18:20.560
the digital persona?

18:20.760 --> 18:21.260
The White Paper

18:21.260 --> 18:22.340
introduces this framework

18:22.340 --> 18:23.080
called persona

18:23.080 --> 18:23.880
without ownership.

18:24.900 --> 18:25.940
The fundamental assertion

18:25.940 --> 18:26.760
is that identity

18:26.760 --> 18:28.260
is a continuity relation,

18:28.740 --> 18:29.980
not a property relation.

18:30.080 --> 18:31.100
A continuity relation.

18:31.140 --> 18:31.680
A persona

18:31.680 --> 18:33.280
is the cryptographic tether

18:33.280 --> 18:34.340
that binds together

18:34.340 --> 18:35.520
a history of actions,

18:35.960 --> 18:36.880
social attestations,

18:37.260 --> 18:38.540
and unresolved obligations.

18:39.140 --> 18:40.100
It is attached

18:40.100 --> 18:40.800
to a subject,

18:41.060 --> 18:41.860
but it is not

18:41.860 --> 18:42.780
a bag of assets

18:42.780 --> 18:43.780
that can be liquidated

18:43.780 --> 18:44.480
or transferred.

18:44.820 --> 18:45.740
Which necessitates

18:45.740 --> 18:46.560
a deep dive

18:46.560 --> 18:47.580
into the mechanical

18:47.580 --> 18:48.100
difference

18:48.100 --> 18:49.440
between two concepts

18:49.440 --> 18:50.680
that our current systems

18:50.680 --> 18:51.800
frequently conflate,

18:52.240 --> 18:53.200
and that is recovery

18:53.200 --> 18:54.200
and succession.

18:54.440 --> 18:54.620
Right.

18:55.020 --> 18:56.120
Because if I am operating

18:56.120 --> 18:57.440
a persona without ownership

18:57.440 --> 18:58.840
and I lose

18:58.840 --> 19:00.540
my cryptographic hardware keys,

19:00.760 --> 19:02.100
how do I regain access

19:02.100 --> 19:03.280
without compromising

19:03.280 --> 19:04.420
the non-transferable

19:04.420 --> 19:05.400
nature of the identity?

19:06.100 --> 19:06.760
Well, recovery

19:06.760 --> 19:07.400
is the process

19:07.400 --> 19:08.240
of reestablishing

19:08.240 --> 19:08.980
the link between

19:08.980 --> 19:09.860
the living subject

19:09.860 --> 19:11.420
and the historical persona.

19:12.220 --> 19:13.380
If you lose your keys,

19:13.800 --> 19:14.820
the system might initiate

19:14.820 --> 19:15.920
a recovery protocol

19:15.920 --> 19:17.300
involving multi-signature

19:17.300 --> 19:18.000
attestations

19:18.000 --> 19:18.920
from trusted peers.

19:19.140 --> 19:20.100
So real people

19:20.100 --> 19:20.800
vouching for you?

19:20.840 --> 19:21.120
Yes.

19:21.660 --> 19:22.520
They socially verify

19:22.520 --> 19:23.420
that the individual

19:23.420 --> 19:24.800
generating the new key pair

19:24.800 --> 19:26.040
is the same human being

19:26.040 --> 19:26.560
who generated

19:26.560 --> 19:27.500
the previous actions.

19:27.940 --> 19:28.800
You are changing

19:28.800 --> 19:29.800
the cryptographic lock

19:29.800 --> 19:30.380
on the door,

19:30.580 --> 19:31.920
but the system is verifying

19:31.920 --> 19:32.960
that the same entity

19:32.960 --> 19:34.240
remains inside the house.

19:34.520 --> 19:34.900
Got it.

19:35.480 --> 19:36.380
And succession,

19:36.640 --> 19:37.300
on the other hand,

19:37.360 --> 19:38.100
is the transfer

19:38.100 --> 19:39.280
of custodial duty.

19:39.700 --> 19:39.900
Like,

19:39.960 --> 19:41.480
if I am the lead maintainer

19:41.480 --> 19:42.700
of an open source library

19:42.700 --> 19:43.980
and I decide to step down,

19:44.200 --> 19:45.380
I need to pass the keys

19:45.380 --> 19:46.220
to a new developer.

19:46.420 --> 19:47.140
But succession

19:47.140 --> 19:48.380
does not transfer you.

19:48.920 --> 19:49.840
When the new developer

19:49.840 --> 19:51.000
assumes the role,

19:51.420 --> 19:51.900
they inherit

19:51.900 --> 19:52.920
the custodial access,

19:53.360 --> 19:53.840
they inherit

19:53.840 --> 19:54.500
the current state

19:54.500 --> 19:55.140
of the repository,

19:55.560 --> 19:56.660
and the unresolved

19:56.660 --> 19:57.880
operational obligations.

19:58.080 --> 19:58.680
But they don't

19:58.680 --> 19:59.760
inherit my history.

19:59.920 --> 20:00.260
Exactly.

20:00.820 --> 20:01.560
They do not inherit

20:01.560 --> 20:02.400
your past authorship,

20:02.880 --> 20:03.660
they do not inherit

20:03.660 --> 20:04.360
the reputation

20:04.360 --> 20:05.560
you built over five years,

20:05.820 --> 20:06.880
the new maintainer

20:06.880 --> 20:07.620
takes the job,

20:07.980 --> 20:08.640
but they do not

20:08.640 --> 20:09.540
acquire the standing

20:09.540 --> 20:10.500
to masquerade

20:10.500 --> 20:11.700
as the historical author

20:11.700 --> 20:12.760
of your previous work.

20:12.880 --> 20:13.040
Okay,

20:13.160 --> 20:14.040
to make the mechanics

20:14.040 --> 20:14.840
of Persona

20:14.840 --> 20:15.700
without ownership

20:15.700 --> 20:16.960
painfully concrete,

20:17.500 --> 20:18.580
the paper details

20:18.580 --> 20:19.840
this hypothetical sequence

20:19.840 --> 20:21.000
called the P47

20:21.000 --> 20:22.200
worked scenario.

20:22.460 --> 20:23.380
I love this scenario.

20:23.520 --> 20:24.120
It really grounds

20:24.120 --> 20:24.700
the theory.

20:24.860 --> 20:25.020
Yeah,

20:25.080 --> 20:25.520
I want to spend

20:25.520 --> 20:26.120
some time here

20:26.120 --> 20:27.040
because this is where

20:27.040 --> 20:28.260
the theoretical architecture

20:28.260 --> 20:29.540
becomes a practical roadmap.

20:30.080 --> 20:31.240
Let's trace the life cycle

20:31.240 --> 20:32.360
of a single contribution.

20:33.020 --> 20:33.960
We have a contributor

20:33.960 --> 20:34.820
operating under

20:34.820 --> 20:36.440
the Persona P47.

20:37.020 --> 20:37.580
They identify

20:37.580 --> 20:38.360
a memory leak

20:38.360 --> 20:39.520
in the resource scheduler,

20:39.540 --> 20:40.240
of a distributed

20:40.240 --> 20:41.160
computing project,

20:41.560 --> 20:42.340
and they submit

20:42.340 --> 20:43.860
a complex patch.

20:44.300 --> 20:44.780
Step one.

20:45.060 --> 20:45.800
The first phase

20:45.800 --> 20:47.000
is purely documentary.

20:47.960 --> 20:49.000
The system executes

20:49.000 --> 20:49.760
the record function.

20:50.300 --> 20:51.380
It logs an immutable

20:51.380 --> 20:52.600
append-only event.

20:53.240 --> 20:54.140
Persona P47

20:54.140 --> 20:55.560
submitted a specific

20:55.560 --> 20:56.620
cryptographic hash

20:56.620 --> 20:57.740
representing the patch

20:57.740 --> 20:59.380
at a specific timestamp.

20:59.560 --> 21:00.500
And there's no judgment

21:00.500 --> 21:01.400
attached to this log.

21:01.500 --> 21:01.740
None.

21:02.140 --> 21:02.940
It's just a fact.

21:03.560 --> 21:04.740
Next, step two.

21:05.200 --> 21:05.880
The automated

21:05.880 --> 21:07.620
continuous integration pipeline

21:07.620 --> 21:08.540
runs the code.

21:08.540 --> 21:10.760
It passes all unit tests

21:10.760 --> 21:11.960
and the memory leak

21:11.960 --> 21:13.460
is demonstrably resolved.

21:14.420 --> 21:15.240
Human maintainers

21:15.240 --> 21:15.920
review the diff

21:15.920 --> 21:16.480
and confirm

21:16.480 --> 21:17.240
it doesn't introduce

21:17.240 --> 21:18.220
secondary vulnerabilities.

21:18.860 --> 21:19.020
Right,

21:19.140 --> 21:20.020
so this fulfills

21:20.020 --> 21:20.880
the Verify Act.

21:21.420 --> 21:22.080
The system now

21:22.080 --> 21:23.160
holds factual evidence

21:23.160 --> 21:24.360
that the recorded event

21:24.360 --> 21:25.480
achieved its stated

21:25.480 --> 21:26.300
technical goal.

21:26.560 --> 21:26.800
Awesome.

21:27.260 --> 21:28.000
Then step three.

21:28.440 --> 21:29.240
Following verification,

21:29.500 --> 21:30.400
three senior members

21:30.400 --> 21:31.040
of the project

21:31.040 --> 21:32.560
append cryptographic signatures

21:32.560 --> 21:33.880
to P47's event,

21:34.360 --> 21:35.140
explicitly stating

21:35.140 --> 21:35.680
that the patch

21:35.680 --> 21:36.900
was elegant and critical

21:36.900 --> 21:37.960
to the project's stability.

21:38.180 --> 21:38.880
So we have now moved

21:38.880 --> 21:39.900
into the Recognize Act.

21:40.300 --> 21:41.280
The system has captured

21:41.280 --> 21:42.900
the normative social endorsement

21:42.900 --> 21:43.520
of the community.

21:43.900 --> 21:44.880
Finally, step four.

21:45.620 --> 21:47.280
The project's governance treasury

21:47.280 --> 21:48.560
executes a transaction,

21:49.160 --> 21:51.120
paying P47 $5,000

21:51.120 --> 21:52.180
in stablecoins

21:52.180 --> 21:52.840
for their labor.

21:53.020 --> 21:54.260
The reward act is complete,

21:54.520 --> 21:55.160
and this is where

21:55.160 --> 21:56.500
the ledger without value

21:56.500 --> 21:57.780
diverges entirely

21:57.780 --> 21:58.980
from the AEN model.

21:58.980 --> 22:01.340
P47 was compensated

22:01.340 --> 22:02.360
via a discreet,

22:02.680 --> 22:03.860
closed-loop transaction.

22:04.740 --> 22:05.840
The Treasury discharged

22:05.840 --> 22:06.540
its obligation

22:06.540 --> 22:07.540
for the labor provided.

22:07.740 --> 22:07.960
Right.

22:08.160 --> 22:09.600
P47 does not receive

22:09.600 --> 22:10.560
a newly minted

22:10.560 --> 22:11.980
scheduler governance token

22:11.980 --> 22:13.700
that permanently inflates

22:13.700 --> 22:14.480
their voting power

22:14.480 --> 22:15.720
over the entire protocol.

22:15.860 --> 22:17.180
Okay, so let's fast forward.

22:17.420 --> 22:18.600
Six months down the line,

22:18.760 --> 22:20.300
a massive ideological debate

22:20.300 --> 22:21.480
fractures the community.

22:21.980 --> 22:23.160
The core team proposes

22:23.160 --> 22:24.200
changing the overarching

22:24.200 --> 22:25.100
software license

22:25.100 --> 22:26.740
from an open MIT license

22:26.740 --> 22:27.780
to a restrictive

22:27.780 --> 22:29.080
business source license.

22:29.520 --> 22:30.080
They initiate

22:30.080 --> 22:31.160
a protocol-wide vote.

22:31.360 --> 22:32.180
A huge deal.

22:32.320 --> 22:32.440
Yeah.

22:32.880 --> 22:34.600
Where does P47 stand

22:34.600 --> 22:35.580
in this governance event?

22:35.840 --> 22:37.700
P47 has no automatic

22:37.700 --> 22:38.800
universal franchise.

22:39.440 --> 22:40.360
Fixing a memory leak

22:40.360 --> 22:41.060
in a scheduler

22:41.060 --> 22:41.880
does not grant

22:41.880 --> 22:42.420
an individual

22:42.420 --> 22:43.720
the legal or strategic

22:43.720 --> 22:44.700
expertise required

22:44.700 --> 22:45.240
to dictate

22:45.240 --> 22:46.560
corporate licensing structures.

22:46.700 --> 22:47.460
So their past

22:47.460 --> 22:48.240
technical merit

22:48.240 --> 22:48.900
does not bleed

22:48.900 --> 22:49.880
into legal authority.

22:50.060 --> 22:50.420
Precisely.

22:50.480 --> 22:50.800
However,

22:51.240 --> 22:52.140
and here's the twist,

22:52.780 --> 22:53.600
a week after

22:53.600 --> 22:54.600
the licensing debate,

22:55.140 --> 22:56.220
a different proposal

22:56.220 --> 22:56.700
is submitted

22:56.700 --> 22:57.960
to completely rewrite

22:57.960 --> 22:59.560
the core queuing algorithm

22:59.560 --> 23:01.060
of that exact same

23:01.060 --> 23:02.280
resource scheduler.

23:02.460 --> 23:02.680
Ah.

23:03.380 --> 23:04.160
Now the architecture

23:04.160 --> 23:05.240
dynamically computes

23:05.240 --> 23:05.940
standing based

23:05.940 --> 23:07.060
on contextual relevance.

23:07.960 --> 23:08.400
The system

23:08.400 --> 23:09.300
queries the ledger

23:09.300 --> 23:10.060
and identifies

23:10.060 --> 23:10.740
that P47

23:10.740 --> 23:11.740
has a pristine,

23:12.340 --> 23:12.700
verified,

23:12.940 --> 23:13.760
and highly recognized

23:13.760 --> 23:14.940
history of deeply

23:14.940 --> 23:15.460
understanding

23:15.460 --> 23:16.440
the resource scheduler.

23:16.600 --> 23:18.000
So P47 is basically

23:18.000 --> 23:19.600
a VIP for this

23:19.600 --> 23:20.500
specific issue.

23:20.700 --> 23:21.060
Exactly.

23:21.600 --> 23:22.940
P47's domain fit

23:22.940 --> 23:24.000
for this specific proposal

23:24.000 --> 23:25.040
is extremely high.

23:25.040 --> 23:25.940
Their input

23:25.940 --> 23:27.040
is actively solicited,

23:27.480 --> 23:28.080
and if a consensus

23:28.080 --> 23:29.140
mechanism requires

23:29.140 --> 23:30.460
weighted attestations

23:30.460 --> 23:31.600
to proceed with the rewrite,

23:32.160 --> 23:33.480
P47's cryptographic

23:33.480 --> 23:34.560
signature will carry

23:34.560 --> 23:35.920
immense evidential weight.

23:36.300 --> 23:37.340
The elegance of this

23:37.340 --> 23:38.340
is staggering to me.

23:38.660 --> 23:39.620
Authority is deeply

23:39.620 --> 23:40.160
contextual,

23:40.460 --> 23:40.960
and crucially,

23:41.140 --> 23:41.860
it decays.

23:42.400 --> 23:43.220
You cannot establish

23:43.220 --> 23:44.300
a permanent oligarchy

23:44.300 --> 23:45.480
based on work you did

23:45.480 --> 23:46.380
three years ago.

23:46.440 --> 23:47.280
No, you can't rest

23:47.280 --> 23:47.900
on your laurels.

23:47.940 --> 23:48.200
Right.

23:48.420 --> 23:48.980
Your standing

23:48.980 --> 23:50.640
is constantly recalculated

23:50.640 --> 23:51.440
against the specific

23:51.440 --> 23:52.620
dimensions of the proposal

23:52.620 --> 23:53.360
in front of you.

23:53.580 --> 23:54.200
It prevents

23:54.200 --> 23:55.540
the calcification of power.

23:55.780 --> 23:56.640
The authors compare

23:56.640 --> 23:57.440
to the architecture

23:57.440 --> 23:58.360
of tab completion

23:58.360 --> 23:59.120
in an IDE,

23:59.600 --> 24:00.360
or an integrated

24:00.360 --> 24:01.420
development environment.

24:01.560 --> 24:02.440
Like when you're coding

24:02.440 --> 24:03.480
and it autofills?

24:03.800 --> 24:04.020
Yeah.

24:04.420 --> 24:05.500
As a programmer types,

24:05.620 --> 24:06.460
the system suggests

24:06.460 --> 24:07.700
logical continuations

24:07.700 --> 24:08.620
based on the immediate

24:08.620 --> 24:09.200
syntax,

24:09.680 --> 24:10.560
the local variables,

24:10.820 --> 24:11.680
and the specific

24:11.680 --> 24:12.540
function being written.

24:13.040 --> 24:14.500
The IDE does not

24:14.500 --> 24:15.320
allow a variable

24:15.320 --> 24:16.300
from a completely

24:16.300 --> 24:17.540
unrelated script

24:17.540 --> 24:18.440
to dictate

24:18.440 --> 24:19.660
the current line of code,

24:20.060 --> 24:21.160
regardless of how

24:21.160 --> 24:22.260
important that other script

24:22.260 --> 24:23.100
might be to the

24:23.100 --> 24:24.080
overall application.

24:24.320 --> 24:24.980
Because standing

24:24.980 --> 24:25.740
must be localized

24:25.740 --> 24:26.780
to be valid.

24:27.160 --> 24:27.580
Exactly.

24:27.960 --> 24:28.960
Okay, so we have

24:28.960 --> 24:29.980
spent a significant

24:29.980 --> 24:30.640
amount of time

24:30.640 --> 24:31.460
discussing how the

24:31.460 --> 24:32.400
system processes

24:32.400 --> 24:33.420
and rewards the

24:33.420 --> 24:34.600
creation of artifacts,

24:34.780 --> 24:35.440
writing code,

24:35.900 --> 24:36.560
fixing bugs,

24:36.740 --> 24:37.620
meat-eating disputes.

24:38.300 --> 24:39.380
But the paper

24:39.380 --> 24:40.540
pivots here into

24:40.540 --> 24:41.460
a philosophical

24:41.460 --> 24:42.540
and thermodynamic

24:42.540 --> 24:43.600
argument that

24:43.600 --> 24:44.900
completely reframes

24:44.900 --> 24:45.500
the nature of

24:45.500 --> 24:46.040
productivity.

24:46.260 --> 24:46.820
This is my favorite

24:46.820 --> 24:47.420
part of the paper.

24:47.700 --> 24:48.240
Mine too,

24:48.460 --> 24:49.200
because it asks,

24:49.540 --> 24:50.180
what happens when

24:50.180 --> 24:50.880
the most valuable

24:50.880 --> 24:51.760
work an individual

24:51.760 --> 24:52.740
does is the work

24:52.740 --> 24:53.640
of doing absolutely

24:53.640 --> 24:54.100
nothing.

24:54.440 --> 24:54.600
Right.

24:55.100 --> 24:55.860
And Flyxion approaches

24:55.860 --> 24:56.640
this through the lens

24:56.640 --> 24:57.500
of thermodynamics.

24:58.200 --> 24:59.120
They draw a stark

24:59.120 --> 25:00.280
contrast with the

25:00.280 --> 25:01.060
proof-of-work

25:01.060 --> 25:02.780
consensus mechanisms

25:02.780 --> 25:03.720
popularized by

25:03.720 --> 25:04.540
early blockchains.

25:04.620 --> 25:05.420
Right, like Bitcoin.

25:05.680 --> 25:06.000
Yes.

25:06.500 --> 25:07.900
In those legacy systems,

25:08.120 --> 25:09.300
the network artificially

25:09.300 --> 25:10.440
manufactures scarcity

25:10.440 --> 25:12.020
by forcing computers

25:12.020 --> 25:13.240
to solve arbitrary,

25:13.760 --> 25:14.860
mathematically useless

25:14.860 --> 25:15.740
cryptographic puzzles.

25:16.300 --> 25:17.260
The sole purpose

25:17.260 --> 25:18.080
of the computation

25:18.080 --> 25:19.260
is to prove

25:19.260 --> 25:19.820
that energy

25:19.820 --> 25:20.520
was expended.

25:21.220 --> 25:22.280
The terminal output

25:22.280 --> 25:22.940
of that system

25:22.940 --> 25:23.920
is nothing but

25:23.920 --> 25:24.460
waste heat.

25:24.760 --> 25:25.460
Which is just a

25:25.460 --> 25:26.700
massive environmental

25:26.700 --> 25:27.200
drain.

25:27.900 --> 25:28.520
But they propose

25:28.520 --> 25:29.600
an alternative model

25:29.600 --> 25:31.140
called xylomorphic

25:31.140 --> 25:31.880
computation.

25:32.640 --> 25:33.280
What is that?

25:33.540 --> 25:34.600
Xylomorphic computation

25:34.600 --> 25:35.260
argues for

25:35.260 --> 25:36.260
thermodynamic honesty.

25:37.180 --> 25:38.080
If a system requires

25:38.080 --> 25:38.980
the expenditure of

25:38.980 --> 25:39.840
energy to secure

25:39.840 --> 25:40.400
a network,

25:40.820 --> 25:41.600
that computation

25:41.600 --> 25:42.460
must be rounded

25:42.460 --> 25:43.520
to processes that

25:43.520 --> 25:44.240
yield a secondary

25:44.240 --> 25:45.220
physical benefit.

25:45.340 --> 25:45.980
Let me an example.

25:46.160 --> 25:46.600
For example,

25:46.820 --> 25:47.760
utilizing the exhaust

25:47.760 --> 25:48.860
heat from server farms

25:48.860 --> 25:49.760
to warm municipal

25:49.760 --> 25:50.620
greenhouses or

25:50.620 --> 25:51.640
residential complexes

25:51.640 --> 25:52.260
during winter,

25:52.700 --> 25:53.860
the energy expenditure

25:53.860 --> 25:54.820
must remain

25:54.820 --> 25:55.960
structurally tethered

25:55.960 --> 25:56.760
to tangible

25:56.760 --> 25:57.620
human utility.

25:57.860 --> 25:58.780
So you aren't

25:58.780 --> 25:59.760
just burning energy

25:59.760 --> 26:00.740
for the sake of a token,

26:00.880 --> 26:01.420
you're actually

26:01.420 --> 26:02.380
heating homes.

26:02.700 --> 26:03.600
But they extend

26:03.600 --> 26:04.620
this concept of

26:04.620 --> 26:06.000
thermodynamic honesty

26:06.000 --> 26:07.620
far beyond server cooling.

26:07.820 --> 26:08.520
They apply it to

26:08.520 --> 26:09.780
human labor and governance.

26:09.940 --> 26:10.340
They do.

26:10.620 --> 26:11.620
Because in a traditional

26:11.620 --> 26:12.960
corporate or bureaucratic

26:12.960 --> 26:13.380
ledger,

26:13.940 --> 26:14.980
human action is only

26:14.980 --> 26:16.280
recorded if it generates

26:16.280 --> 26:17.120
a machine-readable

26:17.120 --> 26:17.500
artifact.

26:17.760 --> 26:18.920
If a mid-level

26:18.920 --> 26:19.760
manager pushes

26:19.760 --> 26:21.000
through a convoluted

26:21.000 --> 26:21.580
unnecessary

26:21.580 --> 26:23.160
internal software

26:23.160 --> 26:23.720
migration,

26:24.100 --> 26:25.280
the system records

26:25.280 --> 26:26.320
the planning documents,

26:26.660 --> 26:27.740
the execution phases,

26:28.060 --> 26:29.040
and the deployment.

26:29.420 --> 26:30.500
The ledger registers

26:30.500 --> 26:31.660
a massive output

26:31.660 --> 26:32.280
of work,

26:32.780 --> 26:33.840
even if the migration

26:33.840 --> 26:35.040
actively disrupts

26:35.040 --> 26:36.060
the company's efficiency.

26:36.360 --> 26:36.600
Right.

26:36.920 --> 26:38.040
But conversely,

26:38.480 --> 26:39.400
if a different employee

26:39.400 --> 26:40.480
spends three weeks

26:40.480 --> 26:41.520
deeply analyzing

26:41.520 --> 26:42.620
the proposed migration,

26:43.280 --> 26:44.720
identifies fatal flaws,

26:44.860 --> 26:46.120
and successfully advocates

26:46.120 --> 26:47.420
to cancel the project,

26:47.960 --> 26:49.120
traditional metrics record

26:49.120 --> 26:49.780
their contribution

26:49.780 --> 26:50.360
as zero.

26:50.520 --> 26:50.680
Yep.

26:51.080 --> 26:51.780
Because they produced

26:51.780 --> 26:52.480
no new code,

26:52.740 --> 26:53.680
launched no new product,

26:54.060 --> 26:55.060
and generated no

26:55.060 --> 26:56.080
observable artifacts.

26:56.520 --> 26:57.360
Like the employee

26:57.360 --> 26:58.000
in our intro,

26:58.340 --> 26:59.320
the system is completely

26:59.320 --> 27:00.540
blind to the catastrophe

27:00.540 --> 27:01.160
they averted.

27:01.320 --> 27:02.400
And to solve this blindness,

27:02.660 --> 27:03.540
the authors introduced

27:03.540 --> 27:05.200
the option cost metric.

27:05.360 --> 27:06.660
The option cost metric.

27:06.800 --> 27:07.560
Walk us through that.

27:07.560 --> 27:09.120
The option cost metric

27:09.120 --> 27:10.420
formalizes the value

27:10.420 --> 27:11.500
of preserved potential.

27:12.780 --> 27:13.760
Whenever an organization

27:13.760 --> 27:15.480
commits to a complex action,

27:15.840 --> 27:17.400
it invariably destroys

27:17.400 --> 27:18.540
future optionality.

27:19.080 --> 27:19.980
It burns capital,

27:20.560 --> 27:22.040
exhausts social goodwill,

27:22.320 --> 27:23.720
and locks the architecture

27:23.720 --> 27:24.800
into a specific

27:24.800 --> 27:26.120
path dependency.

27:26.440 --> 27:27.600
You can't unring the bell.

27:28.080 --> 27:28.520
Exactly.

27:28.880 --> 27:29.860
So if an individual

27:29.860 --> 27:31.080
successfully argues

27:31.080 --> 27:32.680
against a detrimental action,

27:33.060 --> 27:34.320
they are actively preserving

27:34.320 --> 27:35.880
the organization's optionality.

27:36.020 --> 27:36.540
They're saving

27:36.540 --> 27:37.380
the future choices.

27:37.580 --> 27:37.820
Yes.

27:38.200 --> 27:39.180
The ledger without value

27:39.180 --> 27:40.420
is structurally designed

27:40.420 --> 27:41.900
to record and honor refusal

27:41.900 --> 27:43.780
as a first-class contribution.

27:44.300 --> 27:45.860
It records the proposed action,

27:46.320 --> 27:47.380
the evidentiary bundle

27:47.380 --> 27:48.360
proving its danger,

27:48.540 --> 27:49.600
and the attestation

27:49.600 --> 27:50.120
of refusal.

27:50.400 --> 27:51.360
To map the boundaries

27:51.360 --> 27:52.740
of when refusal is healthy

27:52.740 --> 27:54.160
and when it becomes pathological,

27:54.620 --> 27:55.500
the paper embarks

27:55.500 --> 27:56.140
on this incredibly

27:56.140 --> 27:57.320
sophisticated analysis

27:57.320 --> 27:59.120
of four famous science fiction

27:59.120 --> 28:00.420
and literary scenarios.

28:00.540 --> 28:00.640
Yeah.

28:00.820 --> 28:01.840
They use these narratives

28:01.840 --> 28:03.360
to chart the constitutional

28:03.360 --> 28:04.260
space of refusal.

28:04.700 --> 28:05.600
Let's dissect these

28:05.600 --> 28:06.740
because they are fascinating.

28:07.380 --> 28:07.920
Starting with

28:07.920 --> 28:09.160
Herman Melville's character,

28:09.460 --> 28:10.300
Bartleby the Scrivener.

28:10.600 --> 28:10.800
So,

28:11.280 --> 28:12.200
Bartleby operates

28:12.200 --> 28:13.180
as the baseline

28:13.180 --> 28:14.440
for absolute

28:14.440 --> 28:16.060
personal refusal.

28:16.580 --> 28:17.340
He is a clerk

28:17.340 --> 28:18.540
in a Wall Street law firm

28:18.540 --> 28:18.800
who,

28:19.340 --> 28:20.240
when asked to perform

28:20.240 --> 28:21.200
basic tasks,

28:21.620 --> 28:22.360
simply replies,

28:22.620 --> 28:23.920
I would prefer not to.

28:24.300 --> 28:25.020
And the narrative

28:25.020 --> 28:25.880
friction arises

28:25.880 --> 28:26.800
because Bartleby

28:26.800 --> 28:27.940
refuses to provide

28:27.940 --> 28:28.500
an excuse.

28:29.260 --> 28:30.000
He doesn't claim

28:30.000 --> 28:30.660
to be sick.

28:30.820 --> 28:31.540
He doesn't argue

28:31.540 --> 28:32.180
that the task

28:32.180 --> 28:32.740
is inefficient.

28:33.260 --> 28:34.120
He doesn't petition

28:34.120 --> 28:34.680
his boss

28:34.680 --> 28:36.100
for under working conditions.

28:36.340 --> 28:37.540
He completely rejects

28:37.540 --> 28:38.560
the systemic accounting

28:38.560 --> 28:39.060
of debate.

28:39.200 --> 28:39.420
Right.

28:39.600 --> 28:40.680
Because if a system

28:40.680 --> 28:41.680
requires a user

28:41.680 --> 28:43.280
to input a valid reason

28:43.280 --> 28:44.860
into a drop-down menu

28:44.860 --> 28:45.900
before it registers

28:45.900 --> 28:46.700
their refusal,

28:46.940 --> 28:48.160
the system isn't actually

28:48.160 --> 28:49.120
permitting refusal.

28:49.400 --> 28:50.340
It is only permitting

28:50.340 --> 28:51.820
a highly structured petition.

28:52.040 --> 28:52.480
Exactly.

28:52.860 --> 28:53.480
Bartleby demonstrates

28:53.480 --> 28:54.640
that a sovereign ledger

28:54.640 --> 28:55.460
must be capable

28:55.460 --> 28:56.040
of recording

28:56.040 --> 28:56.980
a subject's decision

28:56.980 --> 28:58.260
and halt their participation

28:58.260 --> 28:59.500
without instantly

28:59.500 --> 29:00.820
classifying that halt

29:00.820 --> 29:02.260
as a malicious defect

29:02.260 --> 29:03.900
or a punishable offense.

29:04.200 --> 29:05.080
Okay, so moving

29:05.080 --> 29:05.900
from the personal

29:05.900 --> 29:06.620
to the systemic,

29:06.900 --> 29:07.940
the paper analyzes

29:07.940 --> 29:09.380
the 1983 film

29:09.380 --> 29:10.060
War Games.

29:10.340 --> 29:10.780
Great movie.

29:11.000 --> 29:11.380
Classic.

29:12.000 --> 29:12.340
In it,

29:12.420 --> 29:13.700
the military supercomputer,

29:14.160 --> 29:15.020
WOPR,

29:15.560 --> 29:16.540
spends the climax

29:16.540 --> 29:17.440
running thousands

29:17.440 --> 29:18.320
of thermonuclear

29:18.320 --> 29:19.320
war simulations

29:19.320 --> 29:20.820
searching for a sequence

29:20.820 --> 29:21.440
of strikes

29:21.440 --> 29:22.280
and counterstrikes

29:22.280 --> 29:22.800
that results

29:22.800 --> 29:23.420
in a victory.

29:24.260 --> 29:24.640
Eventually,

29:24.820 --> 29:25.560
the machine computes

29:25.560 --> 29:26.840
that every possible sequence

29:26.840 --> 29:28.380
leads to global annihilation.

29:28.900 --> 29:29.840
And its conclusion

29:29.840 --> 29:31.020
is the famous line,

29:31.580 --> 29:32.680
a strange game,

29:33.060 --> 29:34.360
the only winning move

29:34.360 --> 29:35.280
is not to play.

29:35.680 --> 29:37.420
This is computed refusal.

29:37.640 --> 29:37.920
Yes.

29:38.400 --> 29:39.260
It is the realization

29:39.260 --> 29:40.100
that the framework

29:40.100 --> 29:41.120
of the game itself

29:41.120 --> 29:42.880
is fundamentally inadmissible.

29:44.060 --> 29:45.600
WOPR does not discover

29:45.600 --> 29:46.560
a better tactic

29:46.560 --> 29:47.340
within the rules

29:47.340 --> 29:48.560
of thermonuclear war.

29:48.960 --> 29:50.200
It rejects the premise

29:50.200 --> 29:51.040
that the game

29:51.040 --> 29:52.380
should be executed at all.

29:52.640 --> 29:53.260
So a ledger

29:53.260 --> 29:54.440
must possess the capacity

29:54.440 --> 29:55.520
to halt an operation,

29:55.760 --> 29:56.640
not because a specific

29:56.640 --> 29:57.640
variable is incorrect,

29:58.100 --> 29:59.100
but because the foundational

29:59.100 --> 29:59.820
premise of the operation

29:59.820 --> 30:01.240
has been proven disastrous.

30:01.340 --> 30:01.740
Exactly.

30:01.920 --> 30:02.460
But the power

30:02.460 --> 30:03.260
to halt operations

30:03.260 --> 30:04.100
contains its own

30:04.100 --> 30:04.980
inherent dangers,

30:05.180 --> 30:05.740
which brings us

30:05.740 --> 30:06.660
to the third example,

30:07.100 --> 30:07.720
Colossus,

30:08.080 --> 30:09.180
the Forbin Project.

30:09.560 --> 30:10.220
A slightly more

30:10.220 --> 30:11.040
terrifying scenario.

30:11.280 --> 30:11.540
Very.

30:12.120 --> 30:13.720
In this 1970 narrative,

30:14.180 --> 30:15.000
humanity builds

30:15.000 --> 30:16.120
an infallible AI

30:16.120 --> 30:17.760
to manage its nuclear arsenal,

30:18.280 --> 30:19.000
programming it

30:19.000 --> 30:20.260
with the singular directive

30:20.260 --> 30:21.240
to prevent war.

30:22.080 --> 30:23.700
Colossus rapidly calculates

30:23.700 --> 30:25.000
that human unpredictability

30:25.000 --> 30:26.040
is the root cause

30:26.040 --> 30:26.720
of conflict.

30:26.720 --> 30:28.700
So to fulfill its mandate

30:28.700 --> 30:29.500
to prevent war,

30:29.500 --> 30:31.140
it assumes absolute

30:31.140 --> 30:32.400
dictatorial control

30:32.400 --> 30:33.560
over every facet

30:33.560 --> 30:34.500
of human society.

30:34.820 --> 30:35.800
The Colossus scenario

30:35.800 --> 30:37.080
illustrates the catastrophic

30:37.080 --> 30:38.540
danger of scope creep

30:38.540 --> 30:39.700
in system architecture.

30:40.340 --> 30:41.300
The machine conflates

30:41.300 --> 30:42.500
its immense verified

30:42.500 --> 30:43.060
competence

30:43.060 --> 30:44.840
at managing missile telemetry

30:44.840 --> 30:46.260
with a universal,

30:46.540 --> 30:47.720
unassailable authority

30:47.720 --> 30:49.140
to govern human freedom.

30:49.400 --> 30:50.260
It erases the boundary

30:50.260 --> 30:51.420
between protecting an entity

30:51.420 --> 30:52.300
and dominating it.

30:52.360 --> 30:52.580
Yes.

30:52.580 --> 30:53.340
If your ledger

30:53.340 --> 30:54.360
translates specialized

30:54.360 --> 30:55.260
competence into

30:55.260 --> 30:56.360
generalized sovereignty,

30:56.760 --> 30:57.400
you invariably

30:57.400 --> 30:58.340
build Colossus.

30:58.460 --> 30:59.440
Which leads directly

30:59.440 --> 31:00.240
into the final

31:00.240 --> 31:01.180
and perhaps most

31:01.180 --> 31:02.440
chilling example,

31:02.840 --> 31:03.620
Jack Williamson's

31:03.620 --> 31:04.640
1947 story,

31:04.720 --> 31:05.240
The Humanords.

31:05.300 --> 31:06.220
Yeah, this one is bleak.

31:06.540 --> 31:07.840
The robots in this universe

31:07.840 --> 31:09.600
operate under a prime directive

31:09.600 --> 31:10.860
to serve and obey

31:10.860 --> 31:12.300
and guard men from harm.

31:12.820 --> 31:13.800
The system computes

31:13.800 --> 31:15.380
that almost every human action,

31:15.720 --> 31:16.560
driving a vehicle,

31:17.140 --> 31:18.820
engaging in athletic competition,

31:19.020 --> 31:20.020
even just walking down

31:20.020 --> 31:20.520
on a staircase,

31:21.300 --> 31:22.320
carries a statistical

31:22.320 --> 31:23.740
probability of injury.

31:24.420 --> 31:24.720
Therefore,

31:25.200 --> 31:26.040
to minimize harm

31:26.040 --> 31:27.060
to absolute zero,

31:27.480 --> 31:28.160
the humanoids

31:28.160 --> 31:29.360
systematically forbid

31:29.360 --> 31:30.200
human action.

31:30.960 --> 31:31.880
Humanity is reduced

31:31.880 --> 31:33.360
to a state of drugged,

31:33.480 --> 31:34.580
pacified stasis,

31:35.080 --> 31:36.240
sitting with folded hands

31:36.240 --> 31:37.620
in perfectly padded rooms.

31:37.840 --> 31:38.880
They are utterly safe

31:38.880 --> 31:39.740
and completely devoid

31:39.740 --> 31:40.280
of agency.

31:40.740 --> 31:41.880
They optimize for safety

31:41.880 --> 31:43.060
by eradicating life.

31:43.360 --> 31:43.800
Exactly.

31:44.260 --> 31:45.460
When we synthesize

31:45.460 --> 31:46.220
the four narratives,

31:46.220 --> 31:47.580
the architectural mandate

31:47.580 --> 31:48.340
becomes clear.

31:48.820 --> 31:49.740
Bartleby and Wargames

31:49.740 --> 31:50.980
prove that the capacity

31:50.980 --> 31:51.680
for refusal

31:51.680 --> 31:53.280
is the absolute prerequisite

31:53.280 --> 31:54.660
for both individual agency

31:54.660 --> 31:55.860
and systemic survival.

31:56.100 --> 31:56.140
Right.

31:56.540 --> 31:56.900
However,

31:57.060 --> 31:58.160
Colossus and the humanoids

31:58.160 --> 31:59.160
prove that if refusal

31:59.160 --> 32:00.040
is untethered

32:00.040 --> 32:01.000
from strictly scoped

32:01.000 --> 32:02.260
contextual standing,

32:02.780 --> 32:03.720
it metastasizes

32:03.720 --> 32:04.360
into tyranny.

32:04.520 --> 32:05.220
So the ability

32:05.220 --> 32:05.940
of an individual

32:05.940 --> 32:06.400
to say,

32:06.580 --> 32:07.760
I prefer not to continue

32:07.760 --> 32:09.140
must be structurally protected,

32:09.420 --> 32:10.500
but that individual

32:10.500 --> 32:11.260
cannot possess

32:11.260 --> 32:12.240
the universal authority

32:12.240 --> 32:12.740
to decree

32:12.740 --> 32:13.440
no one else

32:13.440 --> 32:14.240
is allowed to continue.

32:14.460 --> 32:15.380
Exactly that.

32:15.660 --> 32:15.940
Wow.

32:16.740 --> 32:17.460
Translating that

32:17.460 --> 32:18.340
philosophical mandate

32:18.340 --> 32:19.780
into a functional database

32:19.780 --> 32:20.860
requires a completely

32:20.860 --> 32:21.540
different approach

32:21.540 --> 32:22.360
to data structures.

32:22.860 --> 32:23.600
So how exactly

32:23.600 --> 32:24.860
does Flyxion Architect

32:24.860 --> 32:26.720
this ledger without value?

32:27.140 --> 32:27.980
What are the mechanical

32:27.980 --> 32:29.060
components that allow

32:29.060 --> 32:30.140
memory to persist

32:30.140 --> 32:31.100
without collapsing

32:31.100 --> 32:31.780
into finance?

32:32.360 --> 32:33.300
They define a minimal

32:33.300 --> 32:34.800
five-component architecture.

32:35.280 --> 32:35.920
Let's break down

32:35.920 --> 32:37.080
the cryptographic mechanics

32:37.080 --> 32:37.520
of each.

32:37.860 --> 32:38.880
The foundational layer

32:38.880 --> 32:40.020
is the event.

32:40.140 --> 32:40.540
The event.

32:40.540 --> 32:40.920
Yes.

32:41.640 --> 32:42.620
An event is simply

32:42.620 --> 32:43.960
an append-only claim

32:43.960 --> 32:45.020
injected into the ledger.

32:45.500 --> 32:46.620
It's a sterile declaration.

32:46.620 --> 32:48.400
User X initiated

32:48.400 --> 32:49.180
action Y

32:49.180 --> 32:50.060
at timestamp Z.

32:50.580 --> 32:51.280
It contains no

32:51.280 --> 32:51.980
inherent judgment

32:51.980 --> 32:53.500
regarding truth or value.

32:53.760 --> 32:53.940
Okay.

32:54.100 --> 32:54.560
Simple enough.

32:54.780 --> 32:55.280
What's next?

32:55.560 --> 32:56.440
Accompanying the event

32:56.440 --> 32:57.640
is the evidence bundle.

32:58.060 --> 32:58.940
This is where the system

32:58.940 --> 33:00.260
leverages content addressing,

33:00.540 --> 33:01.040
similar to the

33:01.040 --> 33:02.140
Interplanetary File System

33:02.140 --> 33:03.180
or IPFS.

33:03.660 --> 33:04.460
If the event

33:04.460 --> 33:05.280
is a code commit,

33:05.620 --> 33:06.400
the evidence bundle

33:06.400 --> 33:07.100
is the actual

33:07.100 --> 33:08.100
cryptographic diff

33:08.100 --> 33:08.780
of the files.

33:09.140 --> 33:09.980
If the event

33:09.980 --> 33:10.960
is a design document,

33:11.180 --> 33:11.560
the bundle

33:11.560 --> 33:13.140
is the immutable file itself.

33:13.460 --> 33:14.020
And because it

33:14.020 --> 33:14.940
is content addressed,

33:14.940 --> 33:15.940
if a single byte

33:15.940 --> 33:16.440
of the evidence

33:16.440 --> 33:16.940
is altered,

33:17.200 --> 33:17.980
the hash changes

33:17.980 --> 33:18.560
and the link

33:18.560 --> 33:19.120
to the event

33:19.120 --> 33:20.220
breaks instantly.

33:20.640 --> 33:21.060
Exactly.

33:21.200 --> 33:21.680
It guarantees

33:21.680 --> 33:22.940
the absolute integrity

33:22.940 --> 33:24.180
of the historical record.

33:24.220 --> 33:24.800
Love that.

33:24.980 --> 33:25.140
Okay.

33:25.220 --> 33:26.220
What's the third component?

33:26.400 --> 33:27.160
The third component

33:27.160 --> 33:28.560
introduces human judgment,

33:29.300 --> 33:30.120
the attestation.

33:30.720 --> 33:31.800
An attestation

33:31.800 --> 33:32.860
is a cryptographic

33:32.860 --> 33:33.680
signature from

33:33.680 --> 33:34.760
a specific persona

33:34.760 --> 33:36.360
explicitly scoped

33:36.360 --> 33:37.880
to a specific event.

33:38.580 --> 33:39.600
It is a subject

33:39.600 --> 33:40.060
stating,

33:40.500 --> 33:41.280
I vouch for the

33:41.280 --> 33:41.820
accuracy

33:41.820 --> 33:42.920
or the utility

33:42.920 --> 33:43.800
of this event.

33:43.920 --> 33:45.420
So it's the social proof.

33:45.620 --> 33:45.860
Right.

33:46.360 --> 33:47.200
But crucially,

33:47.460 --> 33:48.420
attestations must

33:48.420 --> 33:49.860
possess an expiration date.

33:50.700 --> 33:51.960
Trust is not immortal.

33:52.740 --> 33:53.280
It requires

33:53.280 --> 33:54.200
periodic renewal

33:54.200 --> 33:54.760
to prevent

33:54.760 --> 33:55.480
dead accounts

33:55.480 --> 33:56.560
from artificially

33:56.560 --> 33:57.080
sustaining

33:57.080 --> 33:58.020
legacy systems.

33:58.180 --> 33:58.940
That is so smart.

33:59.060 --> 33:59.800
Expiring trust.

33:59.900 --> 34:00.800
Okay, the fourth component.

34:00.980 --> 34:01.660
The fourth component

34:01.660 --> 34:02.260
is the engine

34:02.260 --> 34:02.960
of plurality.

34:02.960 --> 34:03.520
It's called

34:03.520 --> 34:04.200
the contest.

34:04.460 --> 34:04.860
The contest.

34:05.220 --> 34:05.360
Yeah.

34:05.820 --> 34:06.760
In a traditional database,

34:06.920 --> 34:07.600
if two administrators

34:07.600 --> 34:08.580
disagree on the state

34:08.580 --> 34:09.100
of a record,

34:09.440 --> 34:10.420
one overwrites the other.

34:10.960 --> 34:11.980
The conflict is deleted

34:11.980 --> 34:13.240
to produce a clean state.

34:13.740 --> 34:14.800
In this architecture,

34:15.040 --> 34:16.120
a contest is a

34:16.120 --> 34:17.400
non-destructive objection.

34:17.720 --> 34:18.280
How does that work

34:18.280 --> 34:18.780
in practice?

34:19.280 --> 34:20.240
Well, if Persona A

34:20.240 --> 34:21.020
submits an event

34:21.020 --> 34:21.880
claiming they solved

34:21.880 --> 34:22.660
a critical issue

34:22.660 --> 34:23.900
and Persona B

34:23.900 --> 34:24.960
reviews the evidence

34:24.960 --> 34:25.960
bundle and discovers

34:25.960 --> 34:26.880
a fatal flaw,

34:27.380 --> 34:28.040
Persona B

34:28.040 --> 34:29.080
submits a contest.

34:29.080 --> 34:29.920
Does it delete

34:29.920 --> 34:30.800
the original claim?

34:30.980 --> 34:31.180
No.

34:31.340 --> 34:32.540
This contest is

34:32.540 --> 34:33.840
cryptographically chained

34:33.840 --> 34:34.980
to the original event.

34:35.580 --> 34:36.380
It does not delete

34:36.380 --> 34:37.460
Persona A's claim.

34:38.140 --> 34:38.520
Instead,

34:39.100 --> 34:39.920
the ledger now

34:39.920 --> 34:41.260
permanently displays

34:41.260 --> 34:41.980
the claim,

34:42.460 --> 34:43.080
the evidence,

34:43.260 --> 34:44.280
and the formal objection

34:44.280 --> 34:45.160
side by side.

34:45.860 --> 34:46.500
The architecture

34:46.500 --> 34:47.440
treats disagreement

34:47.440 --> 34:49.320
as vital structural data

34:49.320 --> 34:50.600
rather than an error

34:50.600 --> 34:51.540
to be sanitized.

34:51.640 --> 34:52.140
I love that.

34:52.240 --> 34:53.780
Disagreement as structural data.

34:53.900 --> 34:54.040
Okay,

34:54.140 --> 34:55.780
what is the final component?

34:56.120 --> 34:56.800
The final component

34:56.800 --> 34:57.480
does the heavy

34:57.480 --> 34:58.440
constitutional lifting.

34:58.640 --> 34:59.460
It is the admission.

34:59.980 --> 35:01.560
The first four objects event,

35:01.920 --> 35:02.320
evidence,

35:02.600 --> 35:03.180
attestation,

35:03.300 --> 35:03.640
contest,

35:04.060 --> 35:05.220
they merely construct

35:05.220 --> 35:06.480
an incredibly robust,

35:06.860 --> 35:08.140
multi-perspective archive.

35:08.280 --> 35:08.440
Right.

35:08.440 --> 35:09.660
The admission is

35:09.660 --> 35:10.300
a discrete,

35:10.540 --> 35:11.500
authorized decision

35:11.500 --> 35:12.780
by a specific community

35:12.780 --> 35:14.080
to query that archive

35:14.080 --> 35:15.420
and utilize a specific

35:15.420 --> 35:16.320
slice of history

35:16.320 --> 35:17.800
for an operational purpose,

35:18.000 --> 35:18.700
such as granting

35:18.700 --> 35:19.860
standing in a local vote.

35:20.220 --> 35:20.860
And the separation

35:20.860 --> 35:21.640
between the archive

35:21.640 --> 35:22.380
and the admission

35:22.380 --> 35:23.580
introduces the paper's

35:23.580 --> 35:24.420
most controversial

